{"seq":31,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24579"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish card pp-084, category 2; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Astronomy] What is the sun mostly made up of?\nA. Helium B. Hydrogen C. Uranium\nAnswer: B. Over 70% of the Sun is composed of hydrogen, and most of the remainder is helium. These elements undergo nuclear fusion in the Sun’s core, producing vast amounts of energy that power the Sun and support life on Earth.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/design, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, belief/symbols, ear","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish/pp-084.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"Which chemical element makes up most of the Sun?"},{"field":"de","new":"Aus welchem chemischen Element besteht die Sonne größtenteils?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish","card":"pp-084","category":2}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Astronomy] What is the sun mostly made up of?\nA. Helium B. Hydrogen C. Uranium\nAnswer: B. Over 70% of the Sun is composed of hydrogen, and most of the remainder is helium. These elements undergo nuclear fusion in the Sun’s core, producing vast amounts of energy that power the Sun and support life on Earth."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f05626"}],"hash":"c68981284026"},
